Contract requirements:
- Reset asserted at a rising edge: Reset wins over read and write. Occupancy becomes zero; empty is true and full is false after the edge.
- Write requested while not full: Accept one input word.
- Read requested while not empty: Remove the oldest word. dout holds that word after the edge.
- Read requested while empty: Ignore the read. Nothing is consumed and nothing is bypassed.
- Write requested while full: Ignore the write.
- Read and write between empty and full: Accept both. Occupancy stays constant; the old head is read and the new word joins the tail.
- Read and write while empty: Accept only the write. The new word is not bypassed to dout.
- Read and write while full: Accept only the read. The write is ignored even though the read frees a slot.
- No request: Occupancy and stored words are unchanged.
- Wraparound: Preserve accepted-word ordering and capacity across pointer wraparound.
Checks: {"empty_flag": "empty equals (reference occupancy == 0) after every edge", "full_flag": "full equals (reference occupancy == DEPTH) after every edge", "read_data": "dout equals the reference head removed by an accepted read"}

